    [Doc][Model] Update Kimi-K3 basic, 1M and pooled PD deployment (#18992)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Update the Kimi-K3 guide for eight-node PD and pooled deployment on
    950DT products and Atlas 800I A3, and separate the basic and 1M-context
    instructions.
    
    - Section 5.2 provides complete basic PD templates with `--max-model-len
    262144` (256K) and DCP disabled.
    - Section 5.3 provides complete 1M Prefill/Decode templates and launch
    commands with `--max-model-len 1048576` and Decode DCP8 on 950DT
    products or DCP16 on A3. All other service parameters match the basic
    templates.
    - Recommend enabling Decode DCP when the total input and output length
    is greater than 65536 tokens. The 1M context limit includes input and
    output.
    - Section 5.4 retains the MemCache setup and pooled connectors, uses
    basic 256K templates, and explains the DCP and model-length changes for
    long-context/1M serving. Update section links and the FAQ.
    - Both platforms use Model Runner V2, MooncakeConnectorV2, Prefill
    DP1/PP4, Decode DP4, and memory utilization 0.80. A3 uses TP16 and
    partition `25,25,24,19`; 950DT products uses TP8 and partition
    `24,24,24,21`. Keep A3 KV connector partition metadata on both roles.
    - Document Prefill master/worker ranks, shared master address/port, and
    worker-only `--headless`. Preserve pooled `MultiConnector`,
    `AscendStoreConnector`, MemCache configuration, and lookup identifiers.
    - Consolidate the target model and both DSpark checkpoints into one
    table using the MiniMax-M3 columns: Weight Version, Hardware
    Requirements, Download Links, and Notes. Preserve platform assignments
    and checkpoint URLs.
    - Link the platform-specific DSpark checkpoints, use `A3 series` / `A2
    series` tabs, and consistently name the hardware `950DT products`,
    `Atlas 800I A3`, and `Atlas 800I A2`.
    
    - Use `{{ vllm_ascend_version }}` for all six container images,
    preserving hardware and OS suffixes and leaving shared version
    configuration unchanged.
    
    - Standardize hardware capacity units to `GB` throughout and update the
    KV Cache Pool reference to the current English guide (HTTP 200
    verified).
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Documentation only: reorganize deployment instructions and update
    service examples. Mixed deployment examples remain unchanged by the
    context-section split. No runtime implementation changes.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Final image/256K update: checked all six image references per branch
    use `{{ vllm_ascend_version }}` with the existing platform/OS suffixes.
    Global version values are unchanged. Verified all basic and pooled P/D
    templates use `262144`, while 1M templates retain `1048576`; mixed
    deployment is unchanged. Rendered image variables and checked Bash
    syntax for 48 container/service blocks across both branches.
    
    - Consolidated all documentation changes into one signed-off commit on
    the latest target branch; local rebase onto that branch passes.
    
    - Markdownlint, codespell, typos, and `git diff --check` passed on both
    branches.
    - Before the image/256K update, passed 96 mocked Bash service-template
    scenarios across both branches: basic, 1M, and pooled PD; both
    platforms; Prefill/Decode; ranks 0 through 3. Checked Bash syntax,
    expanded JSON, context length, DCP, tensor parallelism, DSpark settings,
    and Prefill master/worker arguments. No actual vLLM service was
    launched.
    - Compared complete template text: basic and 1M templates differ only in
    maximum model length and Decode DCP. The 1M templates retain the
    previous PD scripts; pooled templates change only those same settings.
    - Verified sections 5.2–5.4 are identical across branches, internal
    anchors resolve, product names and tabs are consistent, mixed deployment
    is unchanged, and MemCache setup is unchanged apart from subsection
    numbering.
    - Attempted `bash format.sh ci` on both branches; actionlint's Go
    dependency download failed with a connection reset. Changed-document
    checks passed separately.
    - No NPU runtime or end-to-end long-context tests were run. Static/mock
    checks do not establish hardware capacity or performance.
    
